# Home Assistant Community App: UniFi OS Server

[![Release][release-shield]][release] ![Project Stage][project-stage-shield] ![Project Maintenance][maintenance-shield]

[![Sponsor Frenck via GitHub Sponsors][github-sponsors-shield]][github-sponsors]

[![Support Frenck on Patreon][patreon-shield]][patreon]

UniFi OS Server allows you to manage your UniFi network using a web browser.

## Important notice

**Experimental production candidate, not a stable release.** This is a breaking
update of the existing app. It retains legacy data and uses Ubiquiti's unchanged
setup wizard for import after in-place MongoDB compatibility preparation.
Read `DOCS.md` and `PRODUCTION_READINESS.md` before any disposable-host test.

## About

This app runs the original UniFi OS Server installer and rootless Podman runtime
inside the existing Home Assistant app. It does not patch vendor binaries or
replace the native backup/restore flow.

ARM64 has been exercised on a disposable HAOS host. AMD64 is defined but still
requires execution validation. Security, option/port compatibility and complete
lifecycle testing remain release blockers.

